      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 11, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"name\": \"SPACE_UNIT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain floor lookup table: one row per floor key with the floor number/label and floor name. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY to attach floor identity to assigned rooms; a lightweight floor reference without the area measures carried by FCLT_FLOOR or FAC_FLOOR.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\", \"name\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Space usage classification lookup table: one row per space usage key with its usage name (e.g. classroom, office, lab usage categories). Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via SPACE_USAGE_KEY to decode the usage classification of assigned rooms.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_USAGE\", \"name\": \"SPACE_USAGE\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Alternative space unit lookup table containing space unit key, code, name, and DLC key, but without the FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution present in SPACE_UNIT. Holds fewer space units than SPACE_UNIT; used when only space unit identity/name is needed without organization linkage.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT2\", \"name\": \"SPACE_UNIT2\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain building lookup table: one row per building with building key/number, building name, street and mailing addresses as single text fields, gross and assignable square footage (in square feet), and a building counter. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via BUILDING_KEY; a lightweight building reference for space-assignment reporting, without the type/ownership/site classification carried by FCLT_BUILDING or FAC_BUILDING.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"BUILDINGS\", \"name\": \"BUILDINGS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"name\": \"Room and Space Inventory\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"name\": \"Space Unit Key\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"name\": \"Building Room Identifier\"}]}"
