      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"table_name\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"count\": 6, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_4562\", \"name\": \"Level-5 Organizations in Top-10 Space Units by Room Count with Dominant Building\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 whose space unit is among the top 10 space units by number of rooms, display the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the count of rooms for each space unit, and the building with the highest number of rooms in that space unit, along with the count of rooms in that building. Order the results by the count of rooms descending and then by space unit key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4025\", \"name\": \"150-Sqft Room Space Unit Max Ranks with Assignable Organization Number Dispersion per HR Department\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a square footage of 150, show the space unit code, space unit name, and the maximum rank within each space unit code group, and for each of those space units, show the major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for each HR department name, considering only organizations that are assignable and have a non-null organization number. The results should include the space unit code, space unit name, maximum rank, major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, average organization number, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2528\", \"name\": \"Stata Building Per-Floor Largest Room with Room-Level Square Footage and Floor Average\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each floor in the Stata building (building 32), what is the largest room square footage and the name of the building room with that largest square footage for rooms loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24 with a largest room square footage greater than 100, and for each space unit on that floor with a room square footage greater than 10, what are the building room name, room number, room square footage, the average room square footage within the floor, and the floor's warehouse load date? List the results showing floor name, largest room name, largest room square footage, building room name, room number, room square footage, average room square footage per floor, and floor warehouse load date, ordered by floor name and room square footage. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2616\", \"name\": \"Large Rooms Above-Average Total Room Counter per Building Room with Floor Count and Space Usage\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each space unit with a room square footage greater than 100, what is the building room, building room name, space usage, the number of distinct floors it appears on, and the total room counter, but only include those where the total room counter is greater than the average room counter across all space units with room square footage greater than 100? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2780\", \"name\": \"Room 21E Windowed Minimum Square Footage with Dual Warehouse Load Dates\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a room number of '21E', show the building room, room square footage, building component, space usage, and the minimum room square footage in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by building key. Also, include the warehouse load date from both the SPACE_DETAIL and SPACE_USAGE tables. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4162\", \"name\": \"Room 21E Windowed Min Square Footage Matched with Access-Level-1 Rooms of the Same Space Unit Code\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a room number of '21E' and for rooms with an access level of 1 in the same space unit code, show the building room, room square footage, building component, space usage, the minimum room square footage in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by building key, the warehouse load date from both the SPACE_DETAIL and SPACE_USAGE tables, the floor, space unit code, space unit name, the average floor within each space unit code group, and the total number of rooms per space unit code. List the results ordered by building room and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
