      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is returning an access-denied error, so direct data verification via `mysql_query` is not possible. However, the semantic network contains an exact-shape precedent metric (`dw_2528`) with fully verified SQL, plus documented column-level evidence (uniqueness of `SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_NAME`, load-date semantics). I'll base the final query on that precedent, adapted to the requested column list.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables**\n- **SPACE_DETAIL** — Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit. Key columns: `BUILDING_KEY` (FK to FCLT_BUILDING; building 32 = Stata), `FLOOR_KEY` (FK to SPACE_FLOOR), `SPACE_UNIT_KEY`, `BUILDING_ROOM`, `BUILDING_ROOM_NAME` (\"name of the building room\"), `ROOM_NUMBER`, `ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE` (square feet), `ROOM_COUNTER`, `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE` (DD-MON-YY text, e.g. '19-DEC-24'; documented: \"all current rows carry '19-DEC-24'\"; this is the *room-side* load date used to filter which room snapshot to analyze).\n- **SPACE_FLOOR** — Space-domain floor lookup: `FLOOR_KEY`, `FLOOR`, `FLOOR_NAME` (documented: unique — 49 distinct names for 49 rows, safe as join/group key), `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE` (floor-lookup load date; distinct from SPACE_DETAIL's).\n- **SPACE_UNIT** — Space unit dimension (`SPACE_UNIT_KEY/CODE/SPACE_UNIT` name, `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`, `DLC_KEY`). Each SPACE_DETAIL row already represents a room assigned to a space unit, so no join is needed to answer \"for each space unit on that floor\".\n- **BUILDINGS** — Space-domain building lookup (building key/number/name, square footages). Not needed: the question filters by building key 32 directly on SPACE_DETAIL, matching the precedent.\n- **FCLT_BUILDING** — Facilities building inventory (square meters, type/site). Not needed for the same reason; also its area units differ (sq m vs sq ft).\n\n**Metrics**\n- **dw_2528** — \"Stata Building Per-Floor Largest Room with Room-Level Square Footage and Floor Average\": identical question shape, with one extra output column (floor warehouse load date). Its verified SQL is the direct template.\n- **dw_2616, dw_2780, dw_4162, dw_4025, dw_4562** — other SPACE_DETAIL-based metrics confirming usage patterns (ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE thresholds, WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE columns, SPACE_USAGE joins).\n- **dw_385** — Stata building (building 32) rooms via FCLT_ROOMS/FCLT_FLOOR (square meters, use descriptions) — the facilities-inventory alternative path.\n\n**Concepts**\n- **concept_room_space_inventory** — groups SPACE_DETAIL / FCLT_ROOMS / FAC_ROOMS / ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD; documents that SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet while FCLT_ROOMS.AREA is in square meters, and that cross-table BUILDING_ROOM matching is unreliable (~2,666 of 9,332/9,872 values overlap).\n- **concept_floor_inventory** — groups FCLT_FLOOR / FCLT_FLOOR_HIST / FAC_FLOOR / SPACE_FLOOR; decision guide: \"Floor name/label for space-assignment reporting → Use SPACE_FLOOR\".\n- **concept_space_unit_dimension**, **concept_building_inventory** — background groupings for SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2 and building tables.\n\n**Column concepts**\n- **column_concept_building_room** — BUILDING_ROOM appears in SPACE_DETAIL, FCLT_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD with different companion columns; SPACE_DETAIL pairs it with ROOM_NUMBER and ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE (sq ft) — exactly the fields the question names.\n- **column_concept_space_unit_key** — SPACE_UNIT_KEY links SPACE_DETAIL rows to space unit identity.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- SPACE_DETAIL joins (graph, outgoing): SPACE_UNIT (SPACE_UNIT_KEY), FCLT_BUILDING (BUILDING_KEY), SPACE_FLOOR (FLOOR_KEY), SPACE_USAGE (SPACE_USAGE_KEY), SPACE_UNIT2, BUILDINGS.\n- SPACE_FLOOR joins (graph): incoming from SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY; member of concept_floor_inventory.\n- Metrics depending on SPACE_DETAIL (metrics_by_table, 6): dw_4562, dw_4025, **dw_2528**, dw_2616, dw_2780, dw_4162.\n- dw_2528 lineage: SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_FLOOR only (no SPACE_UNIT/BUILDINGS join).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (room/floor source candidates)**\n\n| Dimension | SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_FLOOR | FCLT_ROOMS + FCLT_FLOOR | ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per room assigned to a space unit (table desc) | one row per physical room (table desc) | one row per space-planning room record (table desc) |\n| Area measure | ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, **square feet** (concept comparison) | AREA, **square meters** (concept comparison) | **no area column** (concept comparison) |\n| Floor name | SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_NAME (dedicated name column) | FCLT_FLOOR has floor label/sort seq, no FLOOR_NAME | text FLOOR only |\n| Load-date filter | WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE DD-MON-YY '19-DEC-24' documented on both tables | WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE exists but no documented '19-DEC-24' semantics tied to room snapshot | n/a |\n| Building 32 filter | BUILDING_KEY = 32 used in precedent dw_2528 | FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = '32' used in dw_385 | no building key |\n| Fan-out risk | FLOOR_NAME unique (49/49 documented) → safe joins | floor join via (building, floor) pair | no keys to floors |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n\nAtomic requirements: (R1) filter building 32; (R2) filter rooms loaded '19-DEC-24'; (R3) per-floor MAX room square footage > 100 + name of that building room; (R4) rooms with square footage > 10 per floor with building room name, room number, square footage; (R5) average room square footage per floor; (R6) floor name output; (R7) \"square footage\" wording.\n\n- SPACE_DETAIL+SPACE_FLOOR: R1 SUPPORTED (BUILDING_KEY), R2 SUPPORTED (WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE, documented value '19-DEC-24'), R3 SUPPORTED (ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, BUILDING_ROOM_NAME), R4 SUPPORTED (BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, ROOM_NUMBER, ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE all exist), R5 SUPPORTED (AVG over FLOOR_KEY), R6 SUPPORTED (SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_NAME), R7 SUPPORTED (column literally named ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, sq ft).\n- FCLT_ROOMS+FCLT_FLOOR: R2 NOT-SUPPORTED (no documented room-snapshot load-date filter matching '19-DEC-24' semantics), R4 NOT-SUPPORTED (no ROOM_NUMBER/BUILDING_ROOM_NAME pair as named; has ROOM/ROOM_FULL_NAME), R7 VIOLATES semantics (AREA is square meters, not \"square footage\"), R6 NOT-SUPPORTED (no FLOOR_NAME column).\n- ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD: R3/R5/R7 NOT-SUPPORTED (no area measure at all).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"room square footage\" → SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE (exact lexical match, sq ft). Excludes FCLT_ROOMS.AREA (sq m).\n- \"name of the building room\" → SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME (exact match).\n- \"floor name\" → SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_NAME (only floor table with a FLOOR_NAME column).\n- \"loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24\" → SPACE_DETAIL.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24' (column doc explicitly cites this value and this filtering role).\n- \"for each space unit on that floor\" → SPACE_DETAIL rows are already per room-assigned-to-space-unit (table desc); precedent dw_2528 does not join SPACE_UNIT, and no space-unit attribute is requested in the output.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**\n- Same-task-shape precedent: **dw_2528** (1 metric) — identical wording plus one extra column; uses SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_FLOOR, BUILDING_KEY = 32, WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24', thresholds >100 / >10, join on FLOOR_NAME.\n- Other \"Stata building 32\" precedents: dw_385 uses FCLT_ROOMS/FCLCLT_FLOOR — but for square-meter AREA/use-description questions, not square footage.\n- SPACE_DETAIL threshold precedents (>100 sq ft): dw_2616; load-date dual reporting: dw_2780, dw_4162.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- **SPACE_DETAIL**: consumed by 6 metrics (dw_2528, dw_2616, dw_2780, dw_4162, dw_4025, dw_4562) for room-count, room-size, windowed square-footage, and space-unit analyses; grouped under concept_room_space_inventory; decision guide: \"Counting rooms per space unit … Use SPACE_DETAIL\".\n- **SPACE_FLOOR**: joined from SPACE_DETAIL for floor identity; decision guide assigns it the \"floor name/label for space-assignment reporting\" role.\n- **SPACE_UNIT / BUILDINGS / FCLT_BUILDING**: dimensions for space-unit names, building names/areas; not consumed by dw_2528 since no building/space-unit attribute is requested.\n- **dw_2528**: the canonical answer template for this exact question family.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- SPACE_DETAIL — semantic_get, semantic_graph (neighbors, metrics_by_table) ✔\n- SPACE_FLOOR — semantic_get, semantic_graph (neighbors) ✔\n- SPACE_UNIT — semantic_get ✔; BUILDINGS — semantic_get ✔; FCLT_BUILDING — semantic_get ✔\n- dw_2528, dw_2616, dw_2780, dw_385 — semantic_get (full SQL) ✔\n- concept_room_space_inventory, concept_floor_inventory — semantic_get ✔; concept_space_unit_dimension, concept_building_inventory — retrieved via search desc, membership confirmed ✔\n- column_concept_building_room — semantic_get ✔; column_concept_space_unit_key — desc via search + graph edge ✔\n- Remaining Phase-1 hits (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD, FCLT_FLOOR*, FAC_FLOOR, SPACE_USAGE, SPACE_UNIT2, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, etc.) — screened via concept comparisons/decision guides; all non-space-domain hits (subject/library/department entities) discarded as unrelated to rooms/floors.\n- mysql_query verification: **attempted, blocked by database access-denied error (1045)** — noted explicitly; SQL is taken verbatim from the verified precedent dw_2528 with only the removal of the extra load-date column.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use **SPACE_DETAIL** (BUILDING_KEY=32, WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE='19-DEC-24', ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, ROOM_NUMBER, FLOOR_KEY) joined to **SPACE_FLOOR** (FLOOR_KEY → FLOOR_NAME).\n\n**6b.** Follow dw_2528's structure: CTE 1 = per-floor largest room (correlated MAX subquery within building 32 + load date, outer filter >100); CTE 2 = rooms with square footage >10 per floor with AVG over a self-join on FLOOR_KEY (grouped to room grain); final join on FLOOR_NAME (documented unique → no fan